;; Regulatory source register for JPN-FSA payment-services (資金決済法) and
;; financial-regulatory (銀行・金融商品取引・保険) compliance.
;;
;; README.md says: every regulatory claim must cite the official FSA source.
;; docs/business-model.md routes a legal conclusion the governor has not
;; cleared to human sign-off.
;;
;; Until this file existed there was no such list. The documents required a
;; citation against a set that did not exist, so nothing in this repository
;; could tell a real citation from an invented one. This is that list.
;;
;; Shape is tx-data (a vector of entity maps), like every other EDN corpus in
;; this workspace, so it loads with
;;   (d/transact conn (edn/read-string (slurp "facts.edn")))
;; :source/id is the join key. A regulation not in this table has NO
;; spec-basis for this repository -- extend the table, never invent an id, a
;; law id, or a URL.
;;
;; VERIFIED BY `nbb scripts/verify-facts.cljs`, which re-fetches every entry
;; from the live authority. Each entry carries a :source/verify tag naming
;; WHICH check establishes it. The checks are NOT interchangeable, and the
;; reasons are the main thing this file has to teach.
;;
;; Everything below was measured against these hosts on 2026-08-27. The
;; sibling registers in this cohort are written against other agencies and
;; their host notes do not transfer -- this one is www.fsa.go.jp and
;; laws.e-gov.go.jp, and both are wrong in ways that are their own.
;;
;; ── THE 404 PAGE IS BIGGER THAN THE FRONT PAGE
;;
;; Measured 2026-08-27, text with tags and <script> removed:
;;
;;   /zzz-no-such-page-9f3c2a1b8e/   404   3904 chars
;;   /                               200   3241 chars
;;   /common/law/index.html          200   3386 chars
;;   /menkyo/menkyo.html             200   5627 chars
;;
;; Counted by verify-facts.cljs's own de-tag, which is the function that
;; re-measures them on every run. Counting them with a different tool would
;; make the register and its verifier disagree about their own evidence --
;; the numbers below moved by about 200 characters when this was first
;; written with a separate script, purely from how each one strips <script>.
;;
;; The missing page carries the entire global navigation, so it is LONGER
;; than the front page and longer than one of the two pages this register
;; leans on hardest. Every "did I get a real page" heuristic built on size,
;; or on "the body was substantial", gets this host exactly backwards.
;;
;; It is worse than size. The nav carries the ministry's whole subject
;; vocabulary, which is the vocabulary an author reaches for when choosing a
;; needle. Occurrences, measured the same day:
;;
;;                    on 404   on /common/law/index.html
;;   銀行                6            6
;;   保険                6            6
;;   金融商品取引         3            3
;;   法令               10           19
;;   指針               10           18
;;   ガイドライン        12           17
;;   法令・指針等         4            7
;;
;; The first three are IDENTICAL. Every occurrence of 銀行, 保険 and
;; 金融商品取引 on the 法令・指針等 page is chrome -- the page's own body
;; contributes none of them. Those three are precisely the sectors README.md
;; names, so the obvious needle for this repository's subject matter verifies
;; against a deleted page. Even 法令・指針等, which is that page's own title,
;; is on the 404 four times.
;;
;; The page has 3386 characters and only THIRTEEN segments of six characters
;; or more that are not already on the 404. Roughly everything about it is
;; chrome. So needles here are not chosen for topic relevance; they are
;; chosen by set difference against the live 404 body, and the verifier
;; re-does that subtraction every run: a needle found on the fetched 404
;; REFUSES rather than passes.
;;
;; ── THE STATUTE HOST HAS TWO ENDPOINTS THAT DISAGREE ABOUT FABRICATED IDS
;;
;; Measured 2026-08-27, same host, same fabricated id 999AC0000000999:
;;
;;   GET /api/2/law_data/999AC0000000999   -> 404  120 B
;;   GET /api/2/laws?law_id=999AC0000000999 -> 200  {"total_count":0,...}
;;
;; The first discriminates by status. The second does not: a fabricated law
;; id and a real one both answer 200.
;;
;; This matters because the second endpoint is the one you want. It returns
;; 1954 bytes of metadata where law_data returns the full text -- 822 KB for
;; 資金決済法, 4.5 MB for 金融商品取引法. Switching to it is a 400x saving and
;; the obvious optimisation. Made without moving the check off status, it
;; VERIFIES EVERY FABRICATED LAW ID IN THIS FILE, and reports the same
;; "all entries checked" as a run that verified them properly.
;;
;; This register uses the cheap endpoint deliberately, and the checks below
;; never look at its status. They require total_count = 1, the returned
;; law_id to equal the one asked for, and title, number, type and
;; promulgation date to match. That is strictly stronger than the status
;; check it replaces. :law/fabricated-id-control keeps the trap live: it
;; asserts the fabricated id still answers 200 with an empty result, so if
;; this endpoint ever starts 404ing, the note above is stale rather than
;; silently over-cautious.
;;
;; Two smaller shapes of the same endpoint, measured the same day:
;;
;;   an UNKNOWN query parameter is ignored, not rejected -- bogus_param=1
;;   returns 200 and the query runs on the remaining parameters, so a typo in
;;   a filter name silently widens the search instead of failing;
;;
;;   law_title is a SUBSTRING match -- law_title=銀行法 returns 27 laws
;;   including 長期信用銀行法 and 日本銀行法. Nothing in this file is looked up
;;   by title at verification time for that reason; law_id is the key.
;;
;; ── "NOT REPEALED" IS NOT "IN FORCE"
;;
;; Two independent fields, and neither one answers the question alone.
;; Measured 2026-08-27:
;;
;;   324AC0000000068 簡易生命保険法
;;     repeal_status Repeal, repeal_date 2020-04-01, remain_in_force TRUE
;;   329AC0000000115 厚生年金保険法
;;     repeal_status None, current_revision_status PreviousEnforced
;;
;; The first is repealed and still flags remain_in_force, because
;; transitional provisions survive it -- so remain_in_force does not mean
;; what its name suggests. The second is not repealed at all, yet the
;; revision the API serves is not the currently enforced one.
;;
;; So a check that reads only repeal_status passes 厚生年金保険法 while
;; handing back superseded text, and a check that reads only remain_in_force
;; passes a law repealed six years ago. Both fields are asserted separately
;; on every statute here, and both directions are held live by controls:
;; :law/repealed-control (Repeal), :law/previous-enforced-control
;; (None + PreviousEnforced), :law/loss-of-effectiveness-control and
;; :law/expired-control. All four are OUTSIDE this repository's subject
;; matter and are cited for no proposition -- they exist so the repeal and
;; revision checks are checks rather than constants.
;;
;; Three repeal tokens are observed in this corpus -- Repeal, Expire and
;; LossOfEffectiveness -- each with a control below. The set is measured, not
;; assumed, and :host/repeal-tokens is asserted against the controls each run.
;;
;; ── A MISSING PDF IS 36 KB OF HTML
;;
;; The registry lists are PDFs. A deleted one answers:
;;
;;   404, content-type text/html, 36032 B, body = the site 404 page
;;
;; Status is honest here, but "I received a substantial body" is not evidence
;; and neither is "the fetch did not throw". Every PDF below is checked on
;; three independent properties -- status 200, content-type application/pdf,
;; and the %PDF- magic in the first bytes -- so a dead link fails all three
;; and a content-type change fails one and is reported rather than absorbed.
;;
;; Each PDF also asserts that the registry page still LINKS to it. A file
;; that survives while the page that cited it stops pointing at it is an
;; orphaned citation, which is exactly the state this register exists to
;; prevent, and no check on the file alone can see it.

[;; ── HOSTS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 ;; Declared per host because they do not behave alike, and a check written
 ;; against one of them is wrong about the other. Measured at run time, not
 ;; read off this register.

 {:host/name "www.fsa.go.jp"
  :host/kind :page
  :host/charset "utf-8"
  :host/charset-in-header? false
  :host/missing-status 404
  :host/missing-title "エラー404 お探しのページは存在しません。：金融庁"
  :host/missing-probe "https://www.fsa.go.jp/"
  :host/front-page "https://www.fsa.go.jp/"
  :host/missing-longer-than-front? true
  :host/note
  "Honest 404 by status and by title, and a very large one: the missing page
   carries the full global navigation, so its text is LONGER than the front
   page. Size tells you nothing here and subject keywords tell you less --
   銀行, 保険 and 金融商品取引 appear on it the same number of times as on the
   法令・指針等 page. Needles in this file are chosen by subtracting the 404
   body, and the verifier redoes that subtraction live. Declares charset only
   inside the document; the header is a bare text/html. Pages are UTF-8, but
   the header does not say so, so bodies are decoded with a fatal decoder and
   an undecodable body refuses rather than reporting a missing needle."
  :host/measured "2026-08-27"}

 {:host/name "laws.e-gov.go.jp"
  :host/kind :statute-api
  :host/api-base "https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/api/2/laws?law_id="
  :host/full-text-base "https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/api/2/law_data/"
  :host/live-repeal-token "None"
  :host/repeal-tokens ["Repeal" "Expire" "LossOfEffectiveness"]
  :host/enforced-token "CurrentEnforced"
  :host/fabricated-id-status 200
  :host/note
  "Two endpoints that answer a fabricated law id differently: law_data 404s,
   the laws listing returns 200 with total_count 0. This register uses the
   listing endpoint -- 400x smaller -- and therefore never checks its status.
   Identity is total_count = 1 plus an exact law_id match; being in force is
   repeal_status AND current_revision_status, because neither alone is
   sufficient (see the header). Unknown query parameters are ignored rather
   than rejected, and law_title is a substring match, so nothing here is
   looked up by title."
  :host/measured "2026-08-27"}

